=begin pod

The main tools documentation is available from L<raku.org|https://raku.org/>.  

There are some other tools available, which are listed here.  

=head1 Documentation Tools

=item L<Podlite|https://podlite.org/>: open-source desktop Raku Pod editor and 
viewer for Windows, Linux, and Mac.

=item L<pod6.in|https://pod6.in/>: online Raku Pod (aka pod6) editor.

=head1 Other Tools

=item L<CudaText|https://cudatext.github.io/>: Raku lexer is present in Addon 
Manager

=item L<Kate|https://kate-editor.org/>: A cross-platform text editor part of the 
KDE project

=item L<Notepad++|https://notepad-plus-plus.org/>: A free and open-source source 
code editor for use with Microsoft Windows.

=head1 Deprecated tools

=item L<CommaIDE|https://commaide.com/>: designed specifically for Raku. 
Community edition available for free, additional features and more regular 
updates through paid Supporter Program.   Unfortunately no longer supported.  

=item L<Atom|https://atom.io> had various pieces of Raku support, but has been 
sunsetted in 2022.  

=end pod
